This study examines the semileptonic decay of the doubly charmed baryon $\Xi_{cc}^{++}$ into $\Xi_{c}^{+} e^{+}
u_e$ and $\Sigma_{c}^{++} e^{+}
u_e$ using the light-cone quark model. We derive the relevant form factors and determine the decay widths for these transitions. Specifically, the calculated decay width for the $\Xi_{cc}^{++} ightarrow \Xi_{c}^{+} e^{+}
u_e$ process is $1.06^{+0.14}_{-0.13}$ ps$^{-1}$, while for the $\Xi_{cc}^{++} ightarrow \Sigma_{c}^{++} e^{+}
u_e$ transition it is $0.16^{+0.04}_{+0.02}$ ps$^{-1}$. These results indicate that the $\Xi_{cc}^{++}$ baryon is highly suitable for investigating semileptonic decays within future high-energy colliders.

